body:
### Observed

lavish-axi 0.1.87, macOS, Chromium-based default browser. An agent opens a review, edits the artifact a few times (live reload), then wants to close the review tab when the review ends.

- Before any reload the session tab has `history.length === 1` and `window.close()` from an attached page works.
- After 3 live reloads the same tab has `history.length === 4`. Chromium now refuses `window.close()` ("Scripts may close only the windows that were opened by them"), so the tab stays open.
- On one machine this left 36 finished review tabs that no script could close (52 of 61 browser tabs were Lavish tabs before cleanup; see #373 for the other half of the cause).

### Cause

`src/chrome-client.js` reloads the sandboxed artifact iframe by assigning `frame.src = artifactFrameSrcForLoad(...)` (load path and `loadFrame()`). Assigning a new `src` to an already-loaded iframe creates a joint session-history entry in the top-level tab. Every artifact revision therefore grows the tab's history, and Back also walks through old artifact revisions.

### Fix

Navigate the existing frame with `frame.contentWindow.location.replace(url)` after the first load, and keep `frame.src = url` only for the initial load:

```js
function navigateArtifactFrame(url) {
  try {
    if (frame.getAttribute("src") && frame.contentWindow) {
      frame.contentWindow.location.replace(new URL(url, location.href).href);
      return;
    }
  } catch {}
  frame.src = url;
}
```

Verified locally: after 3 live reloads `history.length` stays `1`, the frame shows the newest revision, and the tab closes. The load-token handshake still works because the navigated URL is identical.

### Ask

Use `location.replace` for artifact reloads (both call sites), so a finished review tab stays closable and Back does not replay old revisions. Happy to send a PR through no-mistakes.
